File name: SCH!LOOP.MP
Path description: Great Pyramid gear retrieval loop.
Path starts: Scorched Cavern.
Path ends: ---
Area of the game: MOdule 6
Level recommendation: N/A (level 30+ recommended for gear retrieval though).
Type of path: Loop
File format: New
Monsters encountered: unsure
Additional information:

This loop is specifically for retrieving your gear if it gets scattered
below the great pyramid (as happens if you die inside the pyramid).

For those who are venturing through the great pyramid, take this advice about
this path from Wulfman (many thanks to him for these):


The inevitable will probably happen to most folks who venture into the
pyramid...
But due to a miracle, you will be able to find your scattered gear with
this loop.
When you die in the pyramid Levels 1-5  if anyone else is standing in
the room... or walks into the room where your deathpile is, it will fall
down to the firepits... likely to more than one of them. No Sweat, but
your search on and auto grab and equip as you walk this loop. covers all
of the firepits and returns to the firepit below the great pyramid UP.

If you die in Pharaoh's room and someone is still in the room your gear
is scattered to the deadends at each face of the great pyramid.... a
recovery loop will soon follow, but will be subject to problems
attendant with the recovering gear in the desert.

Suggestion:
take basic store-bought gear with you and drop your good stuff on the
floor... it will drop to the firepits... if you die in Dao Lord room
only your limiteds will survive and be scattered to the four sides of
the pyramid.... the rest... including rare but not limited stuff, like
Sunsword, Elven Silversilk, Astral Robes, Adamantite Platemail....
Cat's-Eye Pendants poof.... gone... oops
Make arrangements with members of your gang to have people run the gear
recovery loop and gather your stuff up while the questing party takes on
the Pharaoh and Dao Lord.

Party - it is possible to party but not recommended in the typical
sense...
if you sent one player through at a time, the first wave to clear the
rooms and open the doors, the subsequent characters to simply run
through, a party could be of great value here, space them out to keep
regen down though. the room clearing players will probably time out and
fall to firepit lvl.